          "message": {
            "text": "Bind the transpiler name helper lexically inside each frame evaluation. The source-run callback retains a free __name call after tsx serialization, while the inspected frame has no module helper; an expression-local identity function closes that transport seam without installing, overwriting, or deleting an authored global in any readable frame. The explicit-headless regression at the related location proves distinct non-function sentinels survive preparation and disposal in both the top document and a same-origin child frame.",
            "markdown": "Bind the transpiler name helper lexically inside each frame evaluation. The source-run callback retains a free __name call after tsx serialization, while the inspected frame has no module helper; an expression-local identity function closes that transport seam without installing, overwriting, or deleting an authored global in any readable frame. The explicit-headless regression at the related location proves distinct non-function sentinels survive preparation and disposal in both the top document and a same-origin child frame."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/capture/scrollbar-capture.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 143,
                  "endLine": 160,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/**\n * Evaluate the discovery callback with esbuild's keep-names helper scoped to\n * this one expression. Source-run `tsx` producers retain free `__name(...)`\n * calls inside the serialized callback, but that module helper does not exist\n * in the inspected frame. A lexical binding avoids installing or deleting a\n * page global, so every readable frame keeps its own authored global state.\n */\nfunction evaluateScrollbarDiscovery<Argument, Result>(\n  frame: Frame,\n  callback: (argument: Argument) => Result | Promise<Result>,\n  argument: Argument,\n): Promise<Result> {\n  const serializedArgument = JSON.stringify(argument);\n  if (serializedArgument == null) {\n    return Promise.reject(new Error(\"scrollbar discovery argument is not JSON-serializable\"));\n  }\n  const expression = `((__name, argument) => (${callback.toString()})(argument))(function(target, value) { try { Object.defineProperty(target, \"name\", { value: value, configurable: true }); } catch {} return target; }, ${serializedArgument})`;\n  return frame.evaluate(expression) as Promise<Result>;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
